  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with the Article III of the SBAA [or the Supplemental Provisions to the Project Document], the responsibility for the safety and security of the Implementing Partner and its personnel and property, and of UNDP&#x2019;s property in the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s custody, rests with the Implementing Partner.  To this end, the Implementing Partner shall: a)	put in place an appropriate security plan and maintain the security plan, taking into account the security situation in the country where the project is being carried; b)	assume all risks and liabilities related to the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s security, and the full implementation of the security plan.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and environmental sustainability will be enhanced through application of the UNDP Social and Environmental Standards (http://www.undp.org/ses) and related Accountability Mechanism (http://www.undp.org/secu-srm).</narrative>
   </condition>
  </conditions>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Level of the legal, planning, policy, institutional and financial frameworks for protected area expansion Strengthened;
2. Number of Protected Areas rehabilited and improved the management system;</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2016">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Gap in ecosystem representation and coverage through a Protected Areas expansion;
2. Lack of capability and resources to manage effectively and minimize threats to the National Parks of Qui&#xe7;ama, Bicuar, Cangandala, Maiombe and Luando Strict Natural Reserve.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. At least 3 community engagement activities contracted and initiated in existing PAs (subsistence activities) and 3 community engagement activities contracted and initiated in proposed PAs (conservation awareness raising)
2. Three dossiers submitted to National Assembly for new PA proclamation
3. Two studies for creation of new PAs completed and stakeholder discussions held
4. The PA system financial sustainability report is received and approved
5. At least one rangers training take place</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 3 communities trained and equipped beekeeping and honey production. Value addition (processing and packaging) and access to formal markets to be explored in 2022.

2. 3 new PA dossiers finalized and pending national level consultation meeting for subsequent submission to the Ministers Cabinet followed by formal submission to the National Assembly.

3. New PAs studies finalized, stakeholders&#x2019; consultations conducted at Municipal and Provincial levels. Completion of the process expected by end of quarter 2 of 2022.

4. Draft financial sustainability study report developed, consultations with specific Protected Areas and their main stakeholders conducted. Some delays due COVID-19 travel restrictions during first 2 quarters of the year affected finalization of the process with final report expected to be delivered by end of quarter 2 of 2022. 

5. 252 rangers (ex-militaries) trained, equipped, and assigned to the specific PAs as per the priorities from the PA Management Authority (National Institute for Biodiversity and Conservation - INBC).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Exchange visit carried out to Gorongosa NP, Mozambique
2. At least 2 community engagement activities contracted and initiated in existing PAs
3.Three studies for creation of new PAs completed and stakeholder discussions held
4. Four national park management plans approved by government</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Four National Parks Management plans approved by INBAC
2. One study for the creation of new PA completed (Cumbira Forest) and one stakeholder discussion held 
3. One ongoing baseline study for community engagement activity is ongoing (tourism Qui&#xe7;ama)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 3 community engagement initiatives operationalized in 3 PAs (beekeeping projects) and lessons learned on community engagement activities captured for MCTA/INBC scale up across the PA system.
2. 3 new PAs dossiers finalized and submitted to National Assembly for official proclamation.
3. Management Plans and community engagement plans developed for 3 new PAs, namely: Cumbira, Morro do Moco and Serra do Pingano.
4. The PA System Financial Sustainability plan finalized.
5. South-south cooperation actions between INBC and similar organizations in the SADC region materialized.
6. Project Terminal Evaluation initiated.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
